{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedCallback.ts#L59","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rate-limiter/useRateLimitedCallback.ts:59"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Preact hook that creates a rate-limited version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rateLimiter"},{"type":"text","value":" function\nthat is exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/pacer"},{"type":"text","value":",\nbut optimized for Preact with reactive options and a stable function reference."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all calls until the limit\nis reached, then blocks subsequent calls until the window resets. Unlike throttling\nor debouncing, it does not attempt to space out or intelligently collapse calls.\nThis can lead to bursts of rapid executions followed by periods where all calls\nare blocked."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rate limiter supports two types of windows:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All executions within the window count\ntowards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'sliding': A rolling window that allows executions as old ones expire. This provides a more\nconsistent rate of execution over time."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For smoother execution patterns, consider:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useThrottledCallback: When you want consistent spacing between executions (e.g. UI updates)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useDebouncedCallback: When you want to collapse rapid calls into a single execution (e.g. search input)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits,\nlike API rate limits or other scenarios requiring hard caps on execution frequency."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook provides a simpler API compared to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRateLimiter"},{"type":"text","value":", making it ideal for basic\nrate limiting needs. However, it does not expose the underlying RateLimiter instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For advanced usage requiring features like:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual cancellation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Access to execution counts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom useCallback dependencies"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRateLimiter"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactRateLimiterOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactRateLimiterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Rate limit API calls to maximum 5 calls per minute with a sliding window\nconst makeApiCall = useRateLimitedCallback(\n  (data: ApiData) => {\n    return fetch('/api/endpoint', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) });\n  },\n  {\n    limit: 5,\n    window: 60000, // 1 minute\n    windowType: 'sliding',\n    onReject: () => {\n      console.warn('API rate limit reached. Please wait before trying again.');\n    }\n  }\n);","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/useRateLimitedCallback.ts:59](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedCallback.ts#L59)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a rate-limited version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic `rateLimiter` function\nthat is exported from `@tanstack/pacer`,\nbut optimized for Preact with reactive options and a stable function reference.\n\nRate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all calls until the limit\nis reached, then blocks subsequent calls until the window resets. Unlike throttling\nor debouncing, it does not attempt to space out or intelligently collapse calls.\nThis can lead to bursts of rapid executions followed by periods where all calls\nare blocked.\n\nThe rate limiter supports two types of windows:\n- 'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All executions within the window count\n  towards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period.\n- 'sliding': A rolling window that allows executions as old ones expire. This provides a more\n  consistent rate of execution over time.\n\nFor smoother execution patterns, consider:\n- useThrottledCallback: When you want consistent spacing between executions (e.g. UI updates)\n- useDebouncedCallback: When you want to collapse rapid calls into a single execution (e.g. search input)\n\nRate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits,\nlike API rate limits or other scenarios requiring hard caps on execution frequency.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useRateLimiter`, making it ideal for basic\nrate limiting needs. However, it does not expose the underlying RateLimiter instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useRateLimiter` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/PreactRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `boolean`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Rate limit API calls to maximum 5 calls per minute with a sliding window\nconst makeApiCall = useRateLimitedCallback(\n  (data: ApiData) => {\n    return fetch('/api/endpoint', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) });\n  },\n  {\n    limit: 5,\n    window: 60000, // 1 minute\n    windowType: 'sliding',\n    onReject: () => {\n      console.warn('API rate limit reached. Please wait before trying again.');\n    }\n  }\n);\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useRateLimitedCallback\ntitle: useRateLimitedCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/useRateLimitedCallback.ts:59](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedCallback.ts#L59)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a rate-limited version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic `rateLimiter` function\nthat is exported from `@tanstack/pacer`,\nbut optimized for Preact with reactive options and a stable function reference.\n\nRate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all calls until the limit\nis reached, then blocks subsequent calls until the window resets. Unlike throttling\nor debouncing, it does not attempt to space out or intelligently collapse calls.\nThis can lead to bursts of rapid executions followed by periods where all calls\nare blocked.\n\nThe rate limiter supports two types of windows:\n- 'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All executions within the window count\n  towards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period.\n- 'sliding': A rolling window that allows executions as old ones expire. This provides a more\n  consistent rate of execution over time.\n\nFor smoother execution patterns, consider:\n- useThrottledCallback: When you want consistent spacing between executions (e.g. UI updates)\n- useDebouncedCallback: When you want to collapse rapid calls into a single execution (e.g. search input)\n\nRate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits,\nlike API rate limits or other scenarios requiring hard caps on execution frequency.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useRateLimiter`, making it ideal for basic\nrate limiting needs. However, it does not expose the underlying RateLimiter instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useRateLimiter` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/PreactRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `boolean`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Rate limit API calls to maximum 5 calls per minute with a sliding window\nconst makeApiCall = useRateLimitedCallback(\n  (data: ApiData) => {\n    return fetch('/api/endpoint', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) });\n  },\n  {\n    limit: 5,\n    window: 60000, // 1 minute\n    windowType: 'sliding',\n    onReject: () => {\n      console.warn('API rate limit reached. Please wait before trying again.');\n    }\n  }\n);\n```\n"}
